g statuses might be stalled upstream, resulting in zero counts.\n3. **Team Inactivity** – It is also possible that the teams have not been assigned work during the reporting window.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Recommendations (Balanced for Both Teams)  \n\n| Recommendation | Rationale |\n|----------------|-----------|\n| **Validate Data Integration** – Confirm that the data feed from Rolo Core and Rolo Edge into the reporting platform is active and correctly mapped. | A technical issue could be suppressing all activity. |\n| **Audit Submission Processes** – Review the workflow for entry creation, approval, and rejection to ensure no steps are inadvertently blocked. | Process bottlenecks can lead to zero recorded entries. |\n| **Set Minimum Reporting Thresholds** – Establish a baseline (e.g., at least one approved entry per week) to trigger alerts when activity falls to zero. | Early warning helps address lapses promptly. |\n| **Engage Team Leads** – Conduct brief interviews with Rolo Core and Rolo Edge managers to verify whether work is occurring but not being logged. | Human insight can uncover non‑technical reasons. |\n| **Implement a Pilot Reporting Cycle** – Run a short, controlled reporting period with manual entry logs to compare against the automated system. | Provides a control dataset to diagnose discrepancies. |\n| **Communicate Findings** – Share this analysis with stakeholders, emphasizing that the current lack of data limits performance insight. | Transparency maintains trust while corrective actions are taken. |\n\n---\n\n### 7. Overall Verdict  \n\nGiven the **complete absence of data** for both Rolo Core and Rolo Edge, no meaningful comparative performance assessment can be made at this time. The primary focus should be on **diagnosing and correcting the data capture or process issues** that have resulted in zero entries, values, and activity indicators. Once reliable data is available, a substantive head‑to‑head analysis—including metric leadership, individual